the defeat of a self-proclaimed God the  imminent death of the warrior nun and an  approaching holy war the ending of  warrior nun season 2 is filled with  unexpected Revelations  sleazy demon Adriel is the big bad of  season two and he makes for an  incredibly Vivid villain his syrupy tone  is perfectly emblematic of his Charming  manipulative and fundamentally deceitful  ways Adriel is a thief who steals the  Halo from Reya a being who rules the  realm on the other side of the portal  disguising himself as a human he is well  on his way to establishing his own  powerful cult when the first Warrior nun  Ariella skillfully tricks him he is  subsequently entombed for a thousand  years when he's freed by Ava and the  order he immediately becomes the leader  of a brand new cult Adriel is the one  responsible for encouraging Dr Jillian  salvias to create a dimensional portal  he lures her top assistant Christian  into his cult and uses technology from  Arctic to focus the prayers of his  followers making him Invincible he  proceeds to use that Tech to perform  apparent Miracles like healing boils  stopping a plague of locusts and  dispelling a fear-causing fog of course  he's also the source of these ills which  he creates using his cutting Edge  gadgets just when it seems like he's  powerful enough to trap Reya and kill  Ava the warrior nun summons the  Monstrous tarasks from the other side  they tear him limp from limb it's a  perfect end Adriel brags that nothing in  the human realm can kill him so Ava  simply brings over the thing he's been  fleeing it remains to be seen if he'll  actually stay dead but it's obvious that  his death unclouds the minds of his  followers  throughout season 2 Ava is in training  to defeat Adriel while she gains more  control over her powers which include  energy blasts and the ability to face  through objects they suddenly fail her  at random times the Halo just sort of  gave out it's not like it was running  out of power it's just like someone  flipped off a switch this is all thanks  to adriel's gigantic cross which acts as  a siphon for mystical energy even  prayers the uncertainty and  rebelliousness Ava demonstrates in  season one are gone as her sisters in  the order of the cruciform sword become  her priority she accepts them and they  accept her Ava resigns herself to the  idea of having to sacrifice her own life  to defeat Adriel Miguel who has returned  from the other side to kill Adriel tells  Ava that he's a bomb and she's the fuse  that will set him off Ava manages to  survive that eventual detonation but  she's mortally wounded in her fight with  Adriel and Lilith after adriel's  destruction she's content to die and  give the Halo to Beatrice but Lilith  suggests putting her through the gate to  the other side no one knows how this  will affect her but it will save her  life Miguel and Lilith both came back  from the other side and were greatly  changed but neither carried the Halo  what will Ava be like when she returns  we don't yet know  character on Warrior none has enjoyed  crazier swerves than sister Lilith her  main ambition in season one is to be the  one who receives the Halo after sister  Shannon is killed when Ava gets it  instead she's Furious and sets out on a  mission to kill her but instead a  monstrous tarasque kills her while she  hunts down Ava surprisingly Lilith not  only returns from the dead but comes  back with terrifying new powers her  demonic Claws and quantum teleportation  make her a powerful Ally for the order  when she returns however Lilith finds  her skin becoming scaly in season two  and turns to Dr Jillian salvias for help  Jillian examines the scales and suspects  a mutation of some kind but is unable to  provide her with any real answers when  Lilith goes to Adriel these slippery  manipulator unlocks her potential this  includes giving her sight that allows  her to see demons as well as huge  bat-like Wings in other words she's a  demon nun adriel's sweet talking preys  on Lilith's jealousy of Ava moreover  there's a kernel of Truth in adriel's  arguments about seeking freedom from a  capricious God who does doesn't answer  prayers he uses this to manipulate her  with Dreadful skill in time she becomes  more than a match for the warrior nun in  the end Lilith sees Adriel as the  monster he truly is and develops her own  agenda thus she warns Beatrice that a  holy war is coming and hopes they're on  the same side  the Betrayal of Father Vincent at the  end of season 1 is a truly wild moment  his story as a former Hitman and  alcoholic who redeems himself in the  priesthood is touching until it's  revealed that he's adriel's biggest  accomplice he betrays the trust of  everyone in the order of the cruciform  sword and continues to act as adriel's  right-hand man in season two Vincent  buys into adriel's rhetoric about  freedom and fighting the oppression of  the church however the more that Adriel  grandstands the more Vincent starts to  have doubts this comes to a head when  Adriel kills the pope father Vincent  grabs the crown of thorns which can  render supernatural beings powerless and  gives it to Ava instead of returning it  to Adriel Ava sees his doubts and  approaches him mother Superion spares  Vincent's life earlier in the season  this act of Mercy winds up helping  everyone as father Vincent AIDS the  order in the final battle against atrial  where the disillusioned priest will go  next is unclear especially since he  takes off his collar in the finale  one of the central plots of season one  is Dr Jillian salvias's attempts to save  the life of her son Michael who has a  rare blood disease notably Michael has  visions of adriel's Tomb the warrior  none and other supernatural phenomena  Jillian creates a mystical gate to send  him to a heaven-like place where he can  be healthy when she finally makes the  gate work young Michael runs through it  and disappears Jillian has no idea how  to get him back at the beginning of  season 2 Ava befriends a young man named  Miguel who opposes Adriel he soon  invites Ava to help him and his  organization very quickly Ava learns  there's much more to Miguel than meets  the eye this becomes especially obvious  when he helps her defeat several  demon-possessed people when he tells  them they're going to go to his home  which is a safe place for them to stay  they find themselves at Jillian's house  it's here that Miguel reveals that he's  her son the tragedy of the situation is  that while Jillian is Overjoyed to see  him alive she's also still in mourning  about the time she lost with him  unbeknownst to her his situation is even  more tragic than it appears to be his  only purpose in returning is to carry  out a suicide mission once again a  character who tries to play God Jillian  in this case is punished for her hubris  one of the most Slow Burn character  developments in Warrior Nan is the  friendship that eventually turns into  love between Ava and sister Beatrice  Beatrice struggles with feelings of  worthlessness and fears of rejection  because she is a lesbian she responds to  these thorny emotions with obsessive  overachieving when Beatrice tells a  story about a warrior nun who was gay  Ava immediately understands that this is  Beatrice's way of coming out to her  their friendship deepens in season 2 as  they both take jobs at a local bar in  Switzerland in an attempt to lay low  Beatrice is trying to train Ava but Ava  has her eye on having fun when Beatrice  tells Ava that she's never had a drink  Ava is determined to get her drunk they  have a great time and dance with each  other at a bar their budding love comes  into sharper focus when it appears that  Ava is dead from a fall before Ava  revives Beatrice cradles her and pours  out her heart as the season continues  Ava knows that their time together is  limited and kisses a shocked Beatrice  before sending Ava to the other side  they have another tender moment but  Beatrice doesn't tell Ava she loves her  until after she crosses over  [Music]  I love you it's clear that this will be  something that propels the action as the  series moves forward as their love story  is an excellent anchor amidst all the  weirdness of warrior none  mother Superion has her own journey in  season two she's a stodgy enforcer in  season one disapproving of everything  that Ava does and works closely with  Cardinal du ready to keep the order of  the cruciform sword viable however she  comes around and helps the sisters  invade the Vatican at the end of season  one season two sees her truly come to  grips with her past she reveals the full  story of how she held and was rejected  by the Halo while on a mission her  insistence on working alone wound up  getting the previous mother superian  killed her arrogance made the Halo drop  out of her body and sister Shannon  became her replacement this makes her  resentful of Shannon and even more  resentful of Ava later when Superion is  gunned down she confesses her jealousy  to Ava and the others Ava forgives her  and lies down with her Ava's unconscious  use of the Halo to heal brings Superion  back to life and makes her feel  healthier than she has in years she also  feels closer to the sisters than ever  before having finally admitted to her  festering feelings and personal flaws  one of the most entertaining  relationships in Warrior none is between  sister Yasmin and sister Camilla both of  them start season 2 as secondary  characters who need to prove themselves  and eventually emerge as legitimate butt  kickers in their own ways Camilla is the  youngest member of the order of the  cruciform sword but she's a brilliant  woman whose understanding of Technology  makes her a crucial team member even  when Adriel implants her with a device  that allows him to read her thoughts and  speak to her Camilla manages to turn the  tables on him by getting in his head at  just the right time Yasmin is part of an  order dedicated to protecting the crown  of thorns the weapon that temporarily  deprogrammed Adriel and allowed Ariella  to imprison him when Adriel is let loose  upon the world Yasmin tracks down the  order to inform the warrior nun about  the Crown's existence while guiding them  to the crown in a museum Heist Yasmin  quickly has to figure out how to  navigate the violent and dangerous world  of the order Yasmin and Camilla are key  players in the final battle against  Adriel Camilla takes out a whole gang of  thugs while Yasmin manages to stab one  of the leaders who bleeds out both  likely have even more significant roles  in the future  there are times when it's hard to tell  the difference between the heroes and  villains of warrior none this is  especially true of authority figures and  the show's Pope is no exception in  season one he's Cardinal Francesco  duretti a man obsessed with appearances  who clamps down on the activities of the  order of the cruciform sword because he  doesn't want them making the church look  bad but his manipulations and schemes  make it a little too easy for the order  to suspect that he killed sister Shannon  and tried to get adriel's bones to  consolidate power this suspicion turns  out to be wrong however just because he  didn't do those things doesn't mean he's  not a power hungry and ruthless man he  tortures one of adriel's spies to get  information grandstands at a meeting of  clergy to browbeat them into working  against Adriel and is part of an  institution that has Adriel asserts  killed millions of people throughout its  history the pope is fighting against  Adriel not because it's a righteous  cause but because he's worried about  someone stepping on his Turf next to  Adriel you are his ants  you will nail before him if there's a  God on Earth then what use will people  have for the church Adriel is presented  as a charlatan but he cleverly co-ops  all of the church's rhetoric when do  ready gets disintegrated by Adriel on  live television it's a declaration and  demonstration of power it's horrifying  yet it confirms atrial's claims  one of the last things sister Lilith  says to Sister Beatrice in the season 2  finale is that a dark future awaits them  there's a holy war coming  I really hope you end up on the same  side what exactly does this mean hints  are planted throughout the entire season  the nature of the other side the realm  at the other end of the portal that Dr  Jillian salvius creates is not exactly  clear its existence is first made known  when Adriel arrives on Earth after  ripping open a Gateway from his world  using the Halo he's pursued by terrasks  monstrous demons whose sole purpose is  to regain the mystical object Lilith is  dramatically Changed by her time on the  other side after she's killed and  Jillian sends her over again through the  gate what feels like seconds for Jillian  is days for Lilith who walks through a  desert until she's expelled by an entity  that does not want her there Miguel  wanders the same desert as a boy until  he's rescued by wandering angels and  taken to The Shining City he's raised in  Reyes court and trained as a weapon to  use against Adriel Raya later helps Ava  defeat Adriel is Reya a god demon an  angel or something else entirely is she  going to start the holy war against  Earth or will someone bring the fight to  her what are her motivations and  intentions regarding earth like many of  the most powerful figures on the show  her motivations are inscrutable and  absolutely fascinating
 

